        text: 'At a plant moulding bottle caps, a robot gripper drops caps onto the floor: about 40 stops per shift. You do a 5 whys with the team leader at the machine.\n\nStep 1, why does the gripper drop caps? It grips them off-centre (checked: marks on the dropped caps). Step 2, why off-centre? The caps arrive at a varying position on the conveyor. Step 3, why? The side guide on the conveyor is loose. Step 4, why loose? Its bolts vibrate out. Step 5, why? They have no thread-lock and the weekly check doesn’t include them.\n\nTherefore test, backwards: no thread-lock and no check, therefore loose bolts, therefore a loose guide, therefore caps off-centre, therefore drops. It holds. Countermeasure: thread-lock on the bolts and the guide in the weekly check. Prediction: under 5 stops per shift within a week.',
